{
  "title": "The NetBSD Project",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "NetBSD is a free, fast, secure, and highly portable Unix-like Open Source operating system. It is available for a wide range of platforms, from large-scale servers and powerful desktop systems to handheld and embedded devices.",
      "list_type": null,
      "depth": 0,
      "ordinal": null
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "» Learn more",
      "list_type": null,
      "depth": 0,
      "ordinal": null
    },
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "11.1 available!",
      "list_type": null,
      "depth": 0,
      "ordinal": null,
      "heading_level": 2
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "The NetBSD project is pleased to announce » NetBSD 11.1 «, the first update to the nineteenth major release of NetBSD.",
      "list_type": null,
      "depth": 0,
      "ordinal": null
    },
    {
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "Get NetBSD",
      "list_type": null,
      "depth": 0,
      "ordinal": null,
      "heading_level": 2
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "NetBSD 11.1, released on November 2, 2026. » Release Notes «",
      "list_type": null,
      "depth": 0,
      "ordinal": null
    },
    {
      "kind": "table",
      "text": "CPU | Machines | Install media\namd64 | 64-bit x86-family machines with AMD or Intel CPUs | USB image, DVD, CD\narm | ARM systems like Raspberry Pi, PINE64, ODROID, \"ServerReady\" machines more | Various boards, original RPi\ni386 | 32-bit x86-family generic machines | USB image, DVD, CD\nmips | MIPS systems like EdgeRouter, Loongson, Malta | octeon, mips64el, mipsel\npowerpc | PowerPC systems like Nintendo Wii, DHT Walnut, RouterBOARD | wii, others\nsparc64 | Sun UltraSPARC | DVD, CD\nothers | Amiga, Alpha, Apple PowerPC/68K, Dreamcast, SPARC32, VAX, more architectures | various",
      "list_type": null,
      "depth": 0,
      "ordinal": null
    },
    {
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "A signed list of hashes for the NetBSD 11.1 distribution. The NetBSD Security Officer's PGP key used to sign the list of hashes.",
      "list_type": null,
      "depth": 0,
      "ordinal": null
    },
    {
